Chrome 156 lets a page with an open WebSocket into the back/forward cache and
closes the socket there. Turn that off, so such a page is never cached and its
relay connection is never cut behind the user's back.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5
@@ -2442,7 +2442,6 @@
     },
     {
       name: "DisconnectWebSocketOnBFCache",
-      status: "stable",
     },
     {
       // `kHidden` and `kHiddenButPainting` visibility states are treated as
